stuffed with Marvel in-jokes, easter eggs,

00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:09.980
some Justice League and Wolverine Origins
shade, plus a look at Cable in action as well

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.590
as some other new characters we're getting
in the movie.

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:16.730
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm combing through the Deadpool

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:20.470
2 trailer for easter eggs, gags and other
details you might have missed!

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:25.250
If you're new to my channel I do regular comic-book
movie videos, and I'm kicking off a Deadpool

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.680
giveaway for all my subscribers.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.230
Just leave me a comment about the trailer
and make sure you're subscribed for a chance

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.230
to win!

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.442
And don't forget to listen out for the winner
of my Ant-Man &amp; The Wasp giveaway later in

00:00:35.442 --> 00:00:37.230
this video.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.760
The trailer begins with hints at some of Cable's
origin story.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.650
"I was born into war."

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.380
"Bred into it."

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.270
"People think they understand pain."

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:52.310
"But they have no concept of it."

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:55.870
"What's the most pain you've ever felt?"

00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:01.190
"Maybe the kind that leaves you more machine
than man."

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:05.489
In the comics, Cable is the son of Cyclops
and the Jean Grey-clone Madelyne Prior who

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:13.020
was created by Mr Sinister whose wish was
to use their child as a weapon.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:25.640
And the 
teddy bear on Cable's belt could be a tease

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.880
to Hope Summers, a mutant child who in the
comics Cable believed to be the Mutant Messiah

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.510
who would save both mutants and non-mutants
alike.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:34.510
There was also a "Hope" easter egg in the
Deadpool short "No Good Deed".

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:35.510
I also liked how Cable's gun goes up to eleven
in a hat tip to Spinal Tap's amplifiers which

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:36.510
could be dialled up to eleven.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:38.890
Then of course we get our first fourth-wall
break in the trailer when Deadpool interrupts

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:42.560
to point out Cable's still wearing a green
sleeve in the footage.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.079
"Wait, no stop!"

00:01:45.079 --> 00:01:47.130
"What in the actual ass?!"

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:48.130
"Dale!

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:49.130
What?!

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:50.130
Why?!"

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:51.130
"Why are the visual effects not done?"

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.130
"It's a metal arm!

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.859
It's not like we're trying to remove a moustache."

00:01:53.859 --> 00:01:58.609
The moustache line is an amusing dig at DC's
Justice League and the problems that movie

00:01:58.609 --> 00:02:03.090
had trying to digitally erase Henry Cavill's
moustache which he had to keep during the

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:07.740
Justice League's reshoots due to his contract
for filming Mission: Impossible 6.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.510
On top of that, the fact this early Cable
footage is missing the completed CGI is also

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:17.980
a call-back to the movie X-Men Origins: Wolverine,
which featured Ryan Reynolds as Wade Wilson

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:19.610
aka Deadpool.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:23.830
An unfinished copy of that particular Wolverine
movie, which lacked many of the necessary

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:28.970
visual effects, leaked online a month before
the final film was released in cinemas in

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:30.330
2009.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:34.680
Back in the trailer the Merc with a Mouth
finishes his CGI rant with the line "F***

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.180
it, I'll do it myself!"

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:40.950
Deadpool's words are a nice reference to the
Marvel character Thanos and the end of Avengers:

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:49.209
Age of Ultron where Thanos says "Fine, I'll
do it myself."

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:54.019
Actor Josh Brolin, of course, plays Cable
in Deadpool 2, as well as Thanos in the Marvel

00:02:54.019 --> 00:02:55.690
Cinematic Universe.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:59.480
But that's not the end of this trailer's Thanos
easter eggs and jokes.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:04.091
For example, when Sheriff Deadpool says "I
got the stones to help you" to Cable, it's

00:03:04.091 --> 00:03:08.150
a play on words to do with the fact that Thanos
has long been on the hunt for the Infinity

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:13.209
Stones in the MCU, a mission we'll see him
continue in Avengers: Infinity War.

00:03:13.209 --> 00:03:17.750
Sheriff Deadpool also tells Cable, 'You know,
you're a lot taller in the ...', but he gets

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.260
interrupted.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:23.540
Perhaps the sentence was meant to finish with
the words, 'in the comics' because, unlike

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.370
these toys here, in the books, Cable is taller
than Deadpool.

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:31.599
It could also be a dig at the fact that, in
real life, Josh Brolin is shorter than Ryan

00:03:31.599 --> 00:03:32.599
Reynolds.

00:03:32.599 --> 00:03:37.549
Likewise, it could be another hint at Brolin's
big-screen comic-book role as Thanos, who,

00:03:37.549 --> 00:03:40.019
like Cable, is also very tall.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:45.090
Pixar's Toy Story movies get a big old shout-out
as the toy version of Deadpool not only uses

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:50.060
one of Woody's lines, Reach for the sky!',
but he's also dressed like the much-loved

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:54.310
toy, with a yellow shirt and white buttons,
black and white waistcoat, sheriff's badge,

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:56.390
brown hat, and red neckerchief.

00:03:56.390 --> 00:04:01.030
Notice also how Wade, the name of Deadpool's
alter ego, is inked on the right sole of the

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:06.079
toys' shoes, in a clear a nod to the way Andy
wrote his name on the soles of his toys including

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.079
Woody.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:11.250
Also, the 'E' in Wade is inverted, in a similar
fashion to how the 'N' in Andy is reversed

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.200
in the Toy Story movies.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.000
And did you catch those green toy soldiers
too who also make an appearance in the Toy

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.000
Story films.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.550
Plus, here in the background is Deadpool's
painting from his earlier Wet on Wet teaser.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:28.690
So, now we get to the meat of the trailer
with Cable lining up against a bunch of DMC

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:30.060
security guards.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:35.780
The DMC appear to be the movie version of
the Mutant Response Division, aka MRD, which

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:40.680
have appeared on TV and in the comics as an
anti-mutant elite military group that's captured

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:43.479
and attempted to contain mutants in the Marvel
universe.

00:04:43.479 --> 00:04:48.330
Notice how the style of helmet and uniform
does have some similarities to those of the

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.370
MRD.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:54.250
We also get to see Cable and Deadpool in action
around a DMC truck which appears to have some

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.139
yellow-suited prisoners on board.

00:04:56.139 --> 00:05:00.460
Judging by the electronic restrainers around
their necks, I suspect they may be mutants

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:02.590
that have been imprisoned by the DMC.

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:07.150
We also get a quick look at Julian Dennison's
character who looks like he's an, as-yet,

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:08.480
unnamed mutant.

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:12.680
You might have seen Dennison in director Taika
Waititi's Hunt for the Wilderpeople, but he

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:16.930
also appeared in a quick shot in the teaser
which hinted at some possible fire-based powers

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:18.289
for his character.

00:05:18.289 --> 00:05:23.300
By the way, I think that might also be a toy
of him earlier in Deadpool's Toy Story-inspired

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.389
set.

00:05:24.389 --> 00:05:28.800
Another shot also suggests that Wade Wilson
either gets captured at some point by the

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.860
DMC or he goes undercover as he's wearing
a yellow uniform plus neck restrainer in this

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:35.340
shot of him in prison.

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:39.440
There's also what looks like another set of
villains who may or may not be linked to the

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.440
DMC.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:44.639
Deadpool and Domino go up against some staff
in white uniforms and there are some interesting

00:05:44.639 --> 00:05:50.770
banners in the background which read "Purity
Humanity Infinity" and "Clean Blood Pure Hearts".

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:55.730
This might be a link to The Purifiers who
were another anti-mutant group from the comics.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:06:01.800
The Purifiers were set up by the fanatical
X-Men hater William Stryker and became a quasi-religious

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:06.550
organisation that carried out terrorist attacks
on the mutant population and the X-Men.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:11.200
They may also tie in to Cable's storyline
in the movie as Cable comes from the future

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:15.430
and in the comics has links to the cult-like
Clan Askani.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:20.360
The "Purity Humanity Infinity" banner also
showed up in the Wet on Wet teaser and in

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:25.110
this shot there's also a "The End Is Near"
banner with a picture of a man with an X-logo

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:29.440
plus a cybernetic arm, which could indicate
that it's Cable.

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:33.199
We also get a brief shot of some other new
Deadpool characters.

00:06:33.199 --> 00:06:37.360
On the right is actor Terry Crews from Brooklyn
Nine-Nine, but at the moment we don't know

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.949
for sure what character he's playing in the
film.

00:06:39.949 --> 00:06:41.789
Possibilities include G.W.

00:06:41.789 --> 00:06:46.810
Bridge, Hammer or perhaps another character
who'll appear in a future X-Force movie.

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:51.770
And just behind Deadpool and Crews is someone
who looks like the comic book character Shatterstar

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:56.120
who became part of the X-Force and who seems
to be wearing a similar type of headpiece

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.450
as he did in the comics.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:02.229
There's also a mystery character loading up
a gun who's wearing some very curious skull

00:07:02.229 --> 00:07:03.500
rings on their hand.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:07.750
If you've got any thoughts or theories on
who this might be, let me know in the comments

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:08.750
below.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:12.280
And if you're wondering where Colossus went,
well, he didn't turn up in the main trailer,

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:16.889
but there's an extra scene in an international
trailer which looks like it's in the X-Mansion

00:07:16.889 --> 00:07:19.909
and shows Wade grabbing Colossus's butt.

00:07:19.909 --> 00:07:23.000
And there's a painting of Karl Marx on the
stairway behind them.

